### Mostly yes, but I'd do the move in a lighter form than I wrote. Which shape do you want me to put in TODO.md for "use the CAS for every stored byte"?

**Is it reasonable?** The direction is: one place for every stored byte, everything else referencing it, nothing orphaned. Today that's spread across 7 folders, 3 thumbnail schemes, and per-app upload folders that copy their bytes again into `photos/`. Collapsing that is right.

But the plan I wrote has a weak spot. It makes every picture and recording a **`CONTENT` row**, and `CONTENT`'s read policy only knows documents and mail (`internal/db/policy.go:584`). It would need a new clause for each column that points at it. Some of those columns are private (`PHOTO.original`, `pronunciation_original`), so a mistake there leaks someone's GPS-tagged original. That's real policy work and risk, and what does the row buy for a photo? Its `mime` and `size` are already in GCS's object metadata, and dedupe already comes from naming by hash.

What we actually need from "the CAS" is three things: one folder, named by hash; references by hash; and a sweeper that deletes what nothing references. A row per object isn't required for any of them.

Same real input for each option: `PHOTO` row with `original` = `photos/00521e3d…a6c8.png`, and stock hit `343713c6…101f`, whose picture is stored twice today (`stock/343713c6…101f` and `wiki-images/1645a6d7…b0.jpg`).

- (*) Light: every Blob cell names `content/<hash>`, with no row
  `PHOTO.original` = `content/00521e3d…a6c8`; the object's type is its GCS content-type.
  Stock record `stock/343713c6…101f.json` holds `"picture": "content/1645a6d7…b0"`; a flyer or wiki picture names `content/1645a6d7…b0` the same way.
  The sweeper deletes a `content/` object that no Blob cell, `CONTENT` row, stock record or wiki page names.
  Read access stays exactly as today: `/api/blob/{id}/{column}` checks the cell's own row and column.
  Goes away: `photos/`, `pronunciation/`, `feedback/`, the five app folders, `imageFolders`, the per-app routes, `-thumb.jpg` objects (thumbnails become their own Blob cells, as `PHOTO.thumbnail` already is).
- ( ) Full: every Blob cell becomes a reference to a `CONTENT` row
  `PHOTO.original` = `cntQ3x…` (an ID), pointing at a `CONTENT` row {`hash` 00521e3d…, `blob` `content/00521e3d…a6c8`, `mime` image/png, `size` …}.
  The stock record holds `"picture": "cntR7y…"`.
  The existing content sweeper deletes rows no reference reaches, then their objects.
  Read access: `CONTENT` gets a policy clause for each referencing column (`PHOTO.original`, `PHOTO.crop`, `GROUP.flyer`, `REPORT.screenshot`, …), keeping the private ones private.
  Costs about 7,000 more rows in the documents sheet, and one extra lookup per picture shown.

Either way it's a feature-sized change plus a one-off `local/` migration you'd run after the deploy, so I'd make it **one TODO item** (it replaces the two I added: "Delete media objects no cell names any more" and "Stop keeping the app image folders' upload copies"). Then this task lands as it is:
